# Allowlist strategy: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-include only what the app needs to
# run. This keeps images lean and — crucially — guarantees secrets/, local_storage/,
# *.db backups, dev logs, tests and any future root-level scratch can never leak into
# a built (production) image. Dev still gets the full tree: docker-compose mounts the
# source as a volume at runtime, so tests/conftest/etc. are present when running pytest.
*

# Application code and everything it needs at runtime
!app/
!alembic/
!alembic.ini
!mcp_servers/

# Dependency manifests (Dockerfile copies requirements*.txt before pip install;
# Dockerfile.dev also needs requirements-dev.txt)
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
!pyproject.toml
